    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d988">

                <pb facs="0932" n="920" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg920"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.24/93</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hayter</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the
                        Division of Near Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Alling</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">3475/13/43</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-22">December 22,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Alling</hi>: Many thanks for your letter of
                    December 15th about military supplies to Saudi Arabia. I agree that the
                    modifications you propose are in accordance with our discussions.</p>
                <p>We have had confirmation from London that the authorities there are in agreement
                    with the conclusions reached and are issuing the necessary instructions.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. G. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayter</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
